her_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Steinbeuge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Steinbeuge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Steinbeuge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Steinbeuge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Steinbeuge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Steinbeuge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Steinbeuge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-29T01:25:20Z","updated_at":"2024-10-29T01:28:16Z","body":"Is this fix for only when it enters the scene?\r\nAfter entering the scene, in the event that someone sets the progress to zero, then performs a transform on the path3d then sets it to zero again to update it, will it be updated?\r\nWhat was the problem with the chained calls? It seems like the majority of users expected this as default behaviour, it seems intuitive to me that setting the value is asking for the transform to update by default, no matter the value.\r\n\r\n\r\nCould this all be simplified with an Immediate check box and property ( in the panel with use model front and tilt etc) that makes it behave in the way it did in previous versions?\r\n> We could have a `force_set_progress` function that does this?\r\n\r\nOr this could work too\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2442976660/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]